     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 8000 mg per dose is almost certainly a typo, and it would be dangerous.\n\n- **The dose:** 8000 mg four times daily comes to 32,000 mg a day. The usual adult oral dose is 200\u2013800 mg per dose. The maximum is 3200 mg a day for prescription use, and 1200 mg a day for over-the-counter use. This order is 10 times the maximum daily dose.\n- **The risks:** A dose that high could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity. That is true even for a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg** by mouth four times daily (3200 mg a day). This is the maximum, and it's usually reserved for conditions like inflammatory arthritis.\n- **400 mg** by mouth four times daily (1600 mg a day). This is common for pain or inflammation.\n- **600 mg** by mouth four times daily (2400 mg a day).\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you intended and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the dose with your supervising resident or attending, and take the indication into account. I'd also take food and GI-bleed risk into account when picking the dose."
      }
     ],
