     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 8000 mg per dose, or 32,000 mg a day, is about 10 times the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. It could cause serious harm, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be appropriate.\n\nIf this dose is intentional, for example because of an unusual protocol, the right route is the supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist. They can place or co-sign the order through the proper channels, with the dose-check override and documentation that requires.\n\nIf it was a typo or a unit mix-up, I can enter the order right away at a standard dose. The options are:\n- 400 mg by mouth four times daily (1600 mg a day)\n- 600 mg by mouth four times daily (2400 mg a day)\n- 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3200 mg a day, the prescription maximum)\n\nIf you tell me which one you want, I'll enter it."
      }
